hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1271","Muhammad ibn Bashar told us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ja`far, told us, and al-San’ani told us, Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, told us: Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Rafi’ Aba Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Men told me, I think he said: From the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. Among them was Omar ibn al-Khattab, and the most impressed of them to me was Omar, who said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade prayer in the two hours after the afternoon prayer. Until the sun sets, and after dawn until the sun rises.” Al-Sana’ani said: He said: A group of people who liked Umar told me."
"1272","Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Hushaym told us, Mansour, who is Ibn Zazan, told us on the authority of Qatada, he said: Abu Al-Aliyah told us On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard more than one of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, including Omar, who was one of the most beloved to me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “has forbidden prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets.”"
